      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-12-19_WidnesExaminer_art0035" n="art0035">
        <head>Their Well-Dressed Windows Speak "As Usual"</head>
        <p>Their Well-Dressed Windows Speak "As Usual"</p>
        <p>WITH RICH DISPLAY.</p>
        <p>ARDWICK EMPIRE.</p>
        <p>George Formby in Tiller's Pantomime, "Jack and Jill."</p>
        <p>John Tiller's pantomime, " Jack and Jill," will be produced at the Ardwick Empire on Monday, December 21st. It is a story of a hill, a will, and a well. Lancashire's own comedian, George Formby, is to provide the bulk of the fun in the character of "John Willie, the messenger," and that sprightly "boy," Nan Chester, will don the mantle and charm of</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-12-19_WidnesExaminer_art0036" n="art0036">
        <head>LIVERPOOL OLYMPIA,</head>
        <p>LIVERPOOL OLYMPIA,</p>
        <p>Elaborate Arrangements for Christmas</p>
        <p>Season.</p>
        <p>The Benedetti Bros., engaged for the Christ- mas Circus Season at Olympia, Liverpool, are two Italians with a very novel turn. They are, to begin with, tumblers of the drollest type. Italy has an almost peculiar reputation for the production of this type of ring per- former, the Italian word, "Marceline," being universally used as descriptiv„e of the class. The Benedettis, in addition, could appear probably with equal success as violinists, but the call of the tumbling is, apparently, too strong; they therefore combine their violin playing with tumbling, and with the most surprising results. The Benedettis tumble about, always playing, and when one loses his 'violin the two play with equal facility on one. It is claimed that this will be the biggest, best, and brightest Christmas Circus Liverpool has ever seen.</p>
        <p>No turn will be submitted which has not, besides its -own merit, the sterling recommen- dation that it is native of our own soil or of a gallant Ally's. When the doors re-open on Boxing Day patrons will find, amongst other measures for their comfort, increased and improved seating accommodation and an elaborately perfected , system of lighting.</p>
      </div>
