      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-12-19_WidnesExaminer_art0092" n="art0092">
        <head>Proposal to Create Six Next Wednesday. REQUISITIOI TO THE MAYOR.</head>
        <p>Proposal to Create Six Next Wednesday. REQUISITIOI TO THE MAYOR.</p>
        <p>The following notice has been sent out to the members of the Council:—</p>
        <p>County Borough of Warrington. Town Hall, Warrington, 18th December, 1914.</p>
        <p>In pursuance of a requisition signed by nineteen members of the Council, I hereby convene a Special meeting of the Council to be held on Wednesday next, the 23rd instant, at six o'clock in the evening, at the Town Hall, for the purpose of passing a resolution to confer the Freedom of the Borough, under and pursuant to the Act 48 and 49, Victoria, Cap. 29, on the following gentlemen, viz:— Alderman T. Burton, Alderman W. Bolton, Alderman J. Smethurst, Alderman W. Pier- point, Sir Gilbert Greenall, Bart., C.V.0., and A. H. Crosfield, Esq., in recognition of eminent services rendered by them to the Borough.</p>
        <p>PETER PEACOCK, Mayor. The proposal to be: carried must be supported by two-thirds of the members of the Council present and voting. • The six names will be voted upon as a whole.</p>
        <p>Established 1846. WM. OWEN &amp; SON, FAMILY GROCERS, 15, Sankey Street, Warrington, Beg to inform their numerous Customers that they have the Best Assortment of Xmas Crackers, Chocolates Cryst. Fruit, (Cadbury's &amp;Rowntree's) Biscuits, Dates, Figs, Grapes, Pines That can be produced. PLEASE SHOP EARLY. Telephone 563. Telegrams: 563, Warrington.</p>
      </div>
