        <p>ing the form which made him so useful a front- ranker last season, and it has been deemed ad- visable by the committee to stand him down for a time. • RYLANDS' RECS. v. SPRING VIEW. In the Nokhern Union Cup, second qualify- ing round, at Gorsey-lane; kick-off 2.30 : Rylands' : F. Horrocks; J. Griffiths, A. Hor- rocks, H. Povey and C. Povey; G. Warren and J. Gallop; J. Brandwocd, J. Whittaker, F. Potter, E. Smith, W. Shaw and F. Bagguley. Reserves: A. Rowlinson, A. Penn and J. Dum- bell. CHRISTMAS FOOTBALL. The Yule-tide Holiday Programme. An attractive programme has been arrangedl for the Yule-tide holidays, and will, no doubt, meet with the practical approval of local foot- ball lovers; which practical approval, needless to say, is expressed at the turnstiles, after the usual fashion. On the afternoon of Christmas Day—the kick- Off being timed for 2.3 o—the Wilderspool lads will entertain Leigh—in addition, it is hoped, to entertaining a goodly crowd! Leigh were Warrington's opponents in the opening match of the present season, and a ding-dong game ended in favour of , " our boys" by the odd point in eleven. • On Christmas morning Warrington "A" are due to meet Leigh "A," at Leigh, the start being fixed for 10.30. ' On Boxing Day Warrington's second string will entertain St. Helens Recs. at Wilderspool. On Monday, December 28th, Warrington are engaged to Leeds, in an " away " fixture. This match was down for settlement early on in the season's card, but it had to be postponed owing to, the Wilderspool lads having to play off a tie in the second round of the Lancashire Cup Competition. New Year's Day will see a return visit from Huddersfield. Only one point separated the teams on the occasion of their last meeting, and that important point was in favour of War- rington, who scored 13 to 12. The same day Warrington "A" will play St. Helens "A" at Pill-town. INTERMEDIATE RUGBY LEAGUE. LAST SATURDAY'S RESULTS. At Wilde.rspcol. Parochial 0.8., 17; Wycliffe 0.8., 0. Sacred Heart 0.8., 15; St. Idban's "A," 0. . In Victoria Park. Heathside Froghall, 18; St. Ann's 0.8., 6. Beamont United 0.8., 13; Beamont Ath., 2. 'Arpley-street 0.8., 6; St. Mary's, 5. MATCHES FOR TO-DAY. At Wilderspool. Kick-off 2.15 p.m. St. Alban's "B" v. St. James' Juniors; referee, Mr. J., Cooper. Silver-street 0.8. v. Heathside Froghall; Mr. W. Jones. In Victoria Park. Kick-off 2.15 p.m. St. Barnabas' 0.8. v. St. Alban's "A"; Mr. J. Beardsell. St. James' 0.8. v. Parochial; Mr. It .Williams. Heathside Bewsey 0.8. v. Beamont Athletic; Mr. J. Flynn.</p>
